# What `docker compose build` must NOT bake into the image.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` copied everything in the folder: node_modules
# built for the host, and on a box that has been used, data/users (accounts
# and password hashes), the pinboard, logs, and this machine's local config.
# data/, logs/ and config/ are mounted as volumes at run time anyway, so the
# image needs none of what is in them - except data/seed/, which a fresh
# volume is filled from on first start.

.git
.claude
node_modules
logs
*.log

data/*
!data/seed
!data/queue/.gitkeep
!data/training/.gitkeep
!data/shared-images/.gitkeep

config/*.local.yaml
config/*.local.yaml.*
config/*.bak*
models
taggers
venv
__pycache__
.env

# ── Not for a published image (22 Sep 2026) ──────────────────────────────
#
# The image may go on Docker Hub, so it carries the app and nothing about
# the group's own server or other people's documents.
#
# Working notes, specs and the mockup: the app never reads them, and several
# name this group's server - its addresses, its login, its layout.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
archive/
docs/*
!docs/taggers-setup.md
deploy/
scripts/sync-p40.sh
scripts/sync-z440.sh
scripts/sync.local.env

# MiniMax's official H3 guides and the per-mode files sliced verbatim from
# them. Not ours to redistribute: scripts/docker-start.sh fetches and slices
# them on the machine that runs the container.
prompts/video/h3/references/h3-*.md
